{{also|Wohl|wȯhl|wóhl}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|woll||regional, colloquial; otherwise obsolete}}
* {{alter|de|wol||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wol}}, {{m|gmh|wole}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wola||well}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*wela}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*welh₁-}}. Compare {{cog|nl|wel}}, {{cog|en|well}}, {{cog|da|vel}}, {{cog|sv|väl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/voːl/}}
* {{audio|de|De-wohl.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|oːl}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[possibly]], [[probably]]; as I was told {{gloss|[[modal particle]] expressing an assumption, often like {{m+|en|must}} + infinitive, or {{q|US}} {{m|en|guess}} + clause}}
#: {{uxi|de|{{ux|de|Er ist '''wohl''' schon gegangen.|He '''must''' have left already.}}|'''I guess''' he has left already.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Seine Frau ist '''wohl''' irgendeine bekannte Ärztin.|['''I heard that'''] his wife is some well-known doctor.}}
# [[of course]], [[indeed]] {{gloss|modal particle adding stress to the statement to contradict a preceding one, often like {{m+|en|do}} + infinitive}}
#: {{uxi|de|Du warst ja noch nie in Frankreich.'' − ''Ich war '''wohl''' schon in Frankreich!|"Since you've never been to France..." − "Of course I've been to France!"}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich kann's dir nicht sagen, weil ich's nicht weiß.'' − ''Du weißt es ja '''wohl'''!|"I can't tell you because I don't know." − "But you '''do''' know!"}}
# {{lb|de|regional|north-western Germany}} [[actually]], [[somehow]], [[quite]] {{gloss|modal particle making the statement weaker or expressing a concession}}
#: {{uxi|de|Was habt ihr denn alle mit der Suppe? Ich find die '''wohl''' nicht schlecht.|"Why are you all complaining about the soup? I don't find it all that bad, '''actually'''."}}
# {{lb|de|mostly elevated}} [[well]], [[very well]]
#: {{uxi|de|Ihr habt '''wohl''' gesprochen, mein Herr!|"Ye have spoken '''well''', my lord!"}}
# {{lb|de|regional|_|in|_|Austria|South Tyrol}} in response to a negative question or statement}} [[yes]]; [[surely]]; [[really]]; on the [[contrary]]
#: {{uxi|de|Das stimmt nicht. — '''Wohl'''!|That's not correct. — '''Yes, it is!'''}}
#: {{uxi|de|Kommst du heute Abend nicht? — '''Wohl'''!|Aren't you coming tonight??  — '''Yes, I am!'''}}

====Usage notes====
* The distinction between the strengthening particle (“of course”) and the weakening particle (“actually”) is through intonation. With the former ''wohl'' is strongly stressed, with the latter it is unstressed.
* The weakening particle is regional (as indicated above); more general words for this sense are {{m|de|schon}} or {{m|de|eigentlich}}.

